ATTRIBUTION NOTICE:
The interactive teaching framework used in this course is adapted from Carl Vellotti's
open-source course "Claude Code for Product Managers"
(https://github.com/carlvellotti/claude-code-pm-course), which is licensed under
CC BY-NC-ND 4.0. Copyright (c) 2025 Carl Vellotti. Carl gave explicit written permission
for this adaptation via direct message on 2026-02-22.

Carried over from that work: the per-lesson skill directory layout and slash-command
organisation; the Say:/Check:/Action:/Present it like this: teaching-script markers; the
lesson-file section skeleton (Setup, Your Role, Learning Objectives, Teaching Flow in
Steps, Common Questions, Success Criteria, Sendoff); the shared teaching-rules file that
every lesson reads first; the delivery model in which the learner never touches a terminal
and the agent performs every action; and the role of course-structure.json as the course
manifest.

Original to this repository and authored by danyuchn: all written content, teaching
scenarios and dialogue; the fictional setting (Horizon Academy), the teaching-assistant
persona, and the full cast; every course asset and data file; the Chinese-language
pedagogy rules; the collaboration methodology the course teaches (agent failure modes and
recovery, rather than a tour of product features); the standalone recap and hint skills;
and the removal of all dependencies on the original course's commercial platform.
A full breakdown is in README.md.

